  "summary": {
    "status": "DRAFT - not approved",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Tidewell Freight Services Ltd is a regional road haulage and pallet distribution company based in Estonbridge, incorporated in September 2008, with 46 employees. It is owned by its two directors, Priya Deshmukh (55%) and Thomas Aldred (45%). The company is requesting an increase in its overdraft limit from £200,000 to £275,000 to fund working capital for longer payment terms on a proposed supermarket distribution contract. The existing overdraft is priced at base rate + 3.75% and is next due for review on 30 November 2026.",
      "Revenue fell 4.0% to £3,360,000 in the year ended 30 September 2025 (previous year: £3,500,000). Operating profit fell to £156,000 from £210,000, and net profit after tax was £88,000. Interest cover was 4.0x, unchanged from the previous year and above the covenant minimum of 3.5x.",
      "Total bank borrowing at the year end was £395,000, made up of the overdraft and a vehicle term loan. Cash at bank fell to £41,000 from £88,000; the current ratio was 1.20, above the covenant minimum of 1.10. Trade debtors rose to £612,000 from £540,000 even though revenue fell, which indicates that customers are paying more quickly than last year.",
      "The request would raise the overdraft limit by £75,000 (37.5%) and does not take effect until the Bank confirms credit approval. Compared with last year's review, the differences flagged are lower profit, lower cash and one overdraft excess in the past 12 months (two in the previous review period). No other material changes were identified."
    ],
